00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.890
Let's get back to the story and talk

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:16.010
about what is going on
in the Belgian Congo.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:20.320
So Leopold decided to take
things into his own hands.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.543
With his own money and his own army.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.070
He knew he would need
some support for this

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.810
in terms of just like approval.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.670
So he created an organization,

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:35.020
that he called the
International African Society.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.790
Leopold builds this organization,

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.270
and says that it's meant to be a research

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.900
and philanthropy organization.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.700
With a mission to explore
the world for good

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.130
and for science.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.100
But soon, Leopold would use

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.159
this organization to get his wish of being

00:04:49.159 --> 00:04:51.073
a big boy colonizer.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:56.120
It was 1884 when a bunch
of the European and Ottoman

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.600
and American powers who
were colonizing Africa

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.280
got together and they decided

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.420
that they needed some
sort of a unifying policy

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.400
of how they were going to go into Africa,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.790
how trade was going to work.

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.270
But they wanted to work together

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:10.540
as they carved up the continent of Africa.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.210
Leopold gets up at this conference,

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:13.360
it was in Berlin,

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.879
and he says, listen, I've
got this organization.

00:05:15.879 --> 00:05:19.270
I would love to take this
organization of mine and go

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:23.080
and take over a huge
swath of central Africa.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.840
And everyone's like, you
mean like Belgium is going to

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:25.700
go take over the Congo?

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.940
And he's like, no, no,
no, not Belgium, me.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:29.350
I'll do it with my own money.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.940
And the European powers
are sort of like, okay.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.780
Like how much harm can one
guy and his NGO do going

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.380
into Congo?

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:37.920
So Leopold gets his dream.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.420
He gets international approval
to go take over a swath

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:46.250
of Africa that is 76
times larger than Belgium.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:50.313
He would call his new private
colony, the Congo Free State.

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:53.770
Well, you know what happens next.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.440
He doesn't improve the lives of people.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.710
That was never his intention.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.330
Instead, his army quickly gains control

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.820
over the local population

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:02.520
and starts to use the locals

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:07.410
to forcibly extract raw
materials from the land of Congo.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:10.210
Mainly in rubber, whose price was going up

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.700
during the Industrial Revolution.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.480
And in ivory.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.990
He would put these quotas
on the local people

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:18.760
that they had to get a
certain amount of rubber.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.020
And he would instruct his
army that if they didn't

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.320
bring back their quota,

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:26.420
that they were to go remove
their hands or limbs.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:28.770
This is everyone. Men, women and children

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.110
who are being forced to
work for King Leopold

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.960
and getting their limbs removed

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:34.880
if they don't meet the quota.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.220
So, Leopold starts extracting huge amounts

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:39.050
of wealth from the Congo.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.580
And he uses this new money

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:43.840
to build big shiny things back in Belgium.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.880
Including this big,
beautiful park and archways

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.240
that I used to bike past all the time

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.160
when I lived in Belgium.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.588
Or this beautiful train
station in central Antwerp.

00:06:55.588 --> 00:06:56.421
Wait a minute.

00:06:56.421 --> 00:06:58.265
That train station looks kind of familiar.

00:06:58.265 --> 00:07:01.848
(uplifted whistling music)

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:08.210
Yeah, that's me showing
Henry the clock tower

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.080
in this train station.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:14.110
I had literally no idea that
this train station was built

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:16.883
on the blood of people in the Congo.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:20.700
Okay, so I know you're wondering what is

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.130
this terrible story have anything to do

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:26.510
with vaccines and Johnson
&amp; Johnson and the pandemic?

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:28.283
Here it goes. Buckle up.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:31.710
So while Leopold is doing
all this terrible stuff

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.890
in the late 1800s, almost the 1900s,

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.610
something happens in neighboring Uganda.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:39.000
An epidemic breaks out

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.170
of this mysterious disease
called sleeping sickness.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.320
This is what they called it.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.420
They didn't really know what it was.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.260
But Leopold catches wind of the fact

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:47.810
that there's a disease spreading

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:49.587
into the Congo where he
has all these people,

00:07:49.587 --> 00:07:52.630
and this giant operation
for wealth extraction.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:53.650
And he sort of freaks out.

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:56.860
He's like my whole wealth
operation might get wiped

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:58.710
out by this random epidemic.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.504
So, he decides to put out a cash prize

00:08:01.504 --> 00:08:03.057
for anyone who can go down

00:08:03.057 --> 00:08:06.030
and devise a solution or a remedy

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:07.970
to the sleeping sickness.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:10.770
And then he starts to
invest in actual researchers

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.620
and scientists, to go down to the Congo

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:15.220
and start studying tropical diseases.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.220
To make sure that nothing catches him

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.100
by surprise and wipes out his operation.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.500
Okay, well eventually
the world catches wind

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.970
of all the terrible things
that King Leopold II

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.440
is doing in the Congo.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.440
And they start to mount
pressure against Belgium

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.530
the country, and the actual
government of Belgium

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.310
to put an end to this.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:36.750
It's 1908, and finally
the Belgian government

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.840
is like, dude, stop, like you're done.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.950
And they officially take
Leopold out of the driver's seat

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:45.130
and they annex the Congo for themselves.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.130
And the Congo becomes an
official Belgian colony

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.500
for the first time.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.610
But these scientists and researchers

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.810
who Leopold set up to start looking

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:56.220
into tropical diseases, they didn't leave.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.053
They stayed.

00:08:57.053 --> 00:08:59.130
They kept doing this work
and they actually started

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:01.730
to make some really
important breakthroughs.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:04.500
They establish an official
state run organization

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.050
called the Prince Leopold
Institute for Tropical Medicines.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.370
An institution that was leading the world

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:13.260
in understanding tropical medicines

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:16.730
and teaching research and
study about this topic.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:19.970
This organization was based
permanently in the Congo,

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:21.943
as well as, in Belgium.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:25.410
Fast forward a few years,
and the Congo officially

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:27.730
declares independence from Belgium.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:29.744
- With political independence from Belgium

00:09:29.744 --> 00:09:33.060
control of the entire
Congo was turned over

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.103
to what is called the
Central Congo Government,

00:09:36.103 --> 00:09:38.730
with headquarters in Leopoldville.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:40.810
- By this time, all of the holdovers

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.530
from the King Leopold
days are sort of gone.

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:46.270
And now the Institute
for Tropical Medicine

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:49.110
is actually like a legitimate institute

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:53.130
that is doing groundbreaking,
cutting edge research

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.110
and study on all sorts of pathologies,

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:00.110
and viruses, and parasites
and diseases in this region.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:01.640
They're basically leading the world

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:04.290
in tropical diseases
and understanding them.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:07.030
They moved their headquarters
from Leopold's house

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:09.510
in Brussels to the city of Antwerp where

00:10:10.389 --> 00:10:13.137
that beautiful but
terrible train station is.

00:10:13.137 --> 00:10:15.191
And they sort of turn into like a school,

00:10:15.191 --> 00:10:17.500
like an institution where they're training

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:20.360
researchers to then go out
and work in the real world.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:21.193
Okay. So here's where

00:10:21.193 --> 00:10:24.430
it starts to really
connect with modern day.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.070
You have the Institute
of Tropical Medicine,

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:28.120
which was effectively built

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:33.070
from King Leopold's
operation in the Congo.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.290
A lot of the researchers and students from

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.490
the Institute of Tropical Medicine

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.420
were graduating and moving on

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:42.980
and joining particularly
one pharmaceutical company,

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.460
that was a Belgian pharmaceutical company,

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:45.780
that was down the road from

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.230
the Institute of Tropical Medicine.

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:50.733
This pharmaceutical
company was called Janssen.

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:54.270
And as researchers from

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.360
the Institute of Tropical Medicine

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:59.430
joined Janssen Pharmaceuticals
they continue to do

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.470
that groundbreaking work around the world.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.500
Developing many of the medicines

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:07.750
that the WHO considers
essential medicines.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:11.650
- [Reporter] Vaccines,
serums, medicines, and drugs.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:14.480
- They continue to do work
in the Congo, for example.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.620
Where, just recently,
they developed the vaccine

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.920
for Ebola in the Congo.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.560
- [Female Reporter] A
Belgian doctor was part

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:23.790
of an international team
that was called to Yambuku

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:26.930
in the heart of the
Democratic Republic of Congo.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:28.510
- This is their old stomping grounds

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:32.500
where so much of this
understanding of different viruses,

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:36.050
and parasites, and diseases was founded

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:38.080
during the King Leopold days.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.910
But instead of the colonizing efforts

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:42.770
of the early 1900s, now
these institutions are

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.620
actually doing really good work,

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.823
and actually saving lots of lives.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.754
In 1960 Janssen Pharmaceutical,

00:11:50.754 --> 00:11:52.160
which is full of all

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:55.980
these Institute of Tropical
Medicine researchers,

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.000
gets purchased by

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:00.670
a New Jersey company
called Johnson &amp; Johnson.

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:02.330
- [Announcer] Made only
by Johnson &amp; Johnson,

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:04.392
the most trusted name
in surgical dressings.

00:12:04.392 --> 00:12:07.170
♪ In the language of love ♪

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:10.690
- And yes, this pharmaceutical
company Janssen,

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:13.030
which is now a division
of Johnson &amp; Johnson

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:16.210
was the actual company
that developed the miracle

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.693
COVID-19 vaccine that is
saving the world today.

00:12:19.693 --> 00:12:21.670
- [Reporter] Today,
Janssen Pharmaceutical,

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.804
as part of healthcare
giant Johnson &amp; Johnson

00:12:23.804 --> 00:12:25.232
announced this.

00:12:25.232 --> 00:12:27.284
- The chairman of Janssen, by the way,

00:12:27.284 --> 00:12:32.004
is a graduate of the Institute
of Tropical Medicine.

00:12:32.004 --> 00:12:34.350
Their long legacy in the Congo,

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.360
and their focus on scientific research

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:38.890
around tropical diseases is what gave them

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.860
the capability to be able
to step up to the task

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:45.010
and create a vaccine for COVID-19.

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:49.790
In other words this, led
to this, led to this,

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.860
led to this, led to this.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:54.210
- [Reporter] The first J&amp;J doses expected

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:57.940
to go into American's arms
within 24 to 48 hours.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.490
- Again, we think it's really important

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:00.740
for our country and the world.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:02.110
- Okay. So I know this
sounds like I'm doing

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.147
some sort of like exposé
on Johnson &amp; Johnson

00:13:04.147 --> 00:13:06.700
and Janssen, and they're like dark past.

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:07.880
I'm not.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.120
The work that they're
doing today is amazing.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:12.120
It is saving so many lives.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:14.610
The Institute of Tropical Medicine

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:17.820
is an amazing public health institution

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:20.360
that does really really useful work

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.470
for saving many lives around the world.

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:25.220
And yet, when you trace back the roots

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:26.897
of why this institution exists

00:13:26.897 --> 00:13:29.290
and the original motives for it,

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.043
they're pretty (beep) up.

00:13:32.735 --> 00:13:35.770
- [Female Reporter] His 23
year reign was so brutal

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:37.147
that the population halved,

00:13:37.147 --> 00:13:41.970
while Leopold and his men
amassed huge personal fortune.

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:45.130
- What this story teaches
me is just how impossible

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:50.130
it is to find an institution
that wasn't founded

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.520
on some bloody dark past.

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:56.350
The country I live in, and the
democracy that I am proud of

00:13:56.350 --> 00:14:01.063
is founded on blood of stolen
people from another continent.

00:14:01.933 --> 00:14:04.980
How do I evaluate something
that I think is good

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:07.250
when I really understand
that the backstory

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:11.240
behind it is terrible,
and bloody, and horrific?

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:15.302
The fact that this lifesaving
game-changer vaccine

00:14:15.302 --> 00:14:20.302
has a legacy that is based
on a greedy horrific King

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.290
massacring a bunch of people in the Congo

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:26.800
is a really uncomfortable tension.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.280
But if you look close enough,

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:32.033
it's one that exists in
nearly everything around us.

